{%- doc -%}
  The single server-side decision for the forced-size-selection gate.

  Echoes ONE token, nothing else:

    (empty)  this product is not gated — no size option, a single-value size
             option, or the feature is off
    open     gated, and the shopper's intent is already on the record
    closed   gated, and no size has been chosen

  Both core edit sites capture this rather than re-deriving the condition:
  blocks/buy-buttons.liquid (the wrapper state attributes + the Layer-2
  `disabled` on the hidden input) and blocks/accelerated-checkout.liquid
  (hiding express checkout). Two copies of this Liquid is how the two halves of
  a feature end up disagreeing — the failure mode the card-hover nil-safe
  precedent records, where one half normalised an unset setting
  and the other did not.

  `open` comes from `product_resource.selected_variant` being non-blank, which
  on a PRODUCT PAGE happens only when `?variant=` was in the actual request — a
  shared link, an ad, a collection swatch click (D7 signal 1). It is the same
  signal snippets/bmp-price-variation.liquid:40 already uses to decide whether
  a shopper has chosen, so this is an established convention in this tree
  rather than a new one. Shopify also populates selected_variant by relevance
  in filtered-collection and search contexts (documented at
  snippets/variant-swatches.liquid:78); that is a card surface and never
  reaches the product page, the only surface this gate renders on.

  This snippet READS selected_variant and never writes it — spec §7.4, or
  scripts/check-price-variation.mjs breaks.

  D7 signal 2 (a trusted interaction inside a size control) is a runtime signal
  and lives in assets/bmp-size-required.js. `location.search` is never read at
  runtime: a swatch app pushes `?variant=` into the URL on selection — measured
  again in the §9.1 probe, where clicking Globo's `M` rewrote the URL to
  `?variant=51536967762226` without ever touching the native size radio — so a
  runtime URL read cannot tell a shared link from a client-side rewrite. Only
  the server render can.

  @param {object} product_resource - the product being rendered

  @example
  {%- capture bmp_size_state -%}
    {%- render 'bmp-size-required-state', product_resource: product -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign bmp_size_state = bmp_size_state | strip -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  # Nil-safe: an unmaterialised checkbox reads as nil, and the schema default is
  # true (D3), so nil must mean ON here — otherwise this snippet and
  # snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid would disagree about whether the gate is
  # on for exactly the stores that never opened the Theme Editor (the
  # bmp-card-hover.liquid precedent, which normalises the same way).
  assign bmp_required = true
  if settings.bmp_size_required == false
    assign bmp_required = false
  endif
  assign bmp_size_option = settings.bmp_size_guide_option | strip | default: 'Size'
  assign bmp_gated = false

  if bmp_required
    for bmp_option in product_resource.options_with_values
      if bmp_option.name == bmp_size_option and bmp_option.values.size > 1
        # values.size > 1 mirrors the render half exactly. A size option with
        # ONE value offers nothing to choose: gating it would leave the hidden
        # input[name="id"] disabled forever and break add-to-cart outright on
        # that product.
        assign bmp_gated = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if bmp_gated
    if product_resource.selected_variant != blank
      echo 'open'
    else
      echo 'closed'
    endif
  endif
-%}
